---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Research & Insights | Jess Breathe & Flow"
  description="The research and lived experience behind Jess Breathe and Flow and Sanctuary, why culturally rooted, community-based healing is a public health necessity."
  path="/research-insights"
>
<section class="hero">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 780px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Research & Insights</p>
    <h1>Why this work exists</h1>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">Jess Breathe and Flow, and the Sanctuary space it is building toward, aren't built on intuition alone. They're grounded in public health research, and in original research of our own. Here's the case, in numbers and in findings.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="stat-grid">
      <div class="stat-card">
        <img src={base + "/images/charts/wealth-gap-boston.png"} alt="Median net worth chart: $8 for Black households vs $247,500 for white households in Greater Boston" width="1380" height="1093">
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <img src={base + "/images/charts/life-expectancy-gap.png"} alt="Life expectancy chart: 69 years near Nubian Square in Roxbury vs 92 years in Back Bay" width="1492" height="720">
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card">
        <img src={base + "/images/charts/social-determinants.png"} alt="Donut chart: only 20% of health outcomes come from clinical care, 40% from social and economic factors" width="1143" height="1276">
      </div>
      <div class="stat-card big-number">
        <p class="big-num">15 cigarettes/day</p>
        <p class="big-num-label">The mortality risk of chronic loneliness</p>
        <p class="big-num-source">U.S. Surgeon General, "Our Epidemic of Loneliness and Isolation" (2023)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-inner-light">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 720px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the statistics</p>
    <h2>What our own research found</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">Jessica's graduate research at Pepperdine's Graziadio Business School wasn't background reading for this work. It's the intellectual foundation of it: a qualitative study of 15 Black executive leaders navigating organizational systems not built for them, using Interpretative Phenomenological Analysis.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="thesis-callout">
      <h3>Community as verification infrastructure</h3>
      <p>The study found that when organizations withhold the affirmation people need to feel secure in who they are, Black leaders build what the research calls "verification infrastructure," trusted circles of people who confirm what they see and feel is real. This is the empirical case for healing circles. They are not a nice-to-have. They are the infrastructure people build when institutions fail to provide it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="thesis-callout" style="background: var(--deep-blue);">
      <h3>Stewardship as collective self-repair</h3>
      <p>Leaders who mentor and open doors for others frequently described that work as chosen, not extracted, an intentional act the research ties to Black Consciousness theory's concept of collective self-repair. This is the grounding for a cooperative model: bridging practitioners and community isn't charity. It's a documented form of repair.</p>
      <p class="quote">"We're here. We can exist in these spaces."</p>
    </div>

    <div class="thesis-callout">
      <h3>Financial security and authenticity, an unexpected finding</h3>
      <p>Two participants, independently, described financial security as what made deeper authenticity possible, a finding the original literature review didn't anticipate. It's independent confirmation, from the inside, of what the broader research shows: financial stress is a measurable driver of chronic stress and poor health outcomes. Integrating financial health alongside physical, emotional, and spiritual wellness isn't a scope expansion. It's the same finding, applied.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-tight">
  <div class="wrap center mx-auto" style="max-width: 680px;">
    <p class="eyebrow">Be part of the answer</p>
    <h2>This is a moment that calls for investment, not just attention.</h2>
    <p class="subhead mx-auto">Federal support for community health equity work has been cut sharply since 2025. Local and community-rooted infrastructure is filling the gap right now. Every path below moves this work forward.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href={base + "/experiences"} class="btn btn-primary">Join an Experience</a>
      <a href={base + "/organizations"} class="btn btn-secondary">Partner With Us</a>
      <a href="mailto:info@jessbreatheandflow.com?subject=Investing%20in%20Sanctuary" class="btn btn-secondary">Invest in Sanctuary</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="tint-mist">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="text-align:center; color: var(--inner-light);">Sources</p>
    <ul class="sources-list">
      <li>Federal Reserve Bank of Boston. "The Color of Wealth in Boston." (2015)</li>
      <li>Boston Public Health Commission. "Health of Boston 2023."</li>
      <li>Robert Wood Johnson Foundation / County Health Rankings model, social determinants of health framework.</li>
      <li>U.S. Surgeon General. "Our Epidemic of Loneliness and Isolation." (2023)</li>
      <li>Geronimus, A. et al. "'Weathering' and age patterns of allostatic load scores among blacks and whites in the United States." American Journal of Public Health (2006).</li>
      <li>Moran et al. "Financial Stress and Risk of Coronary Heart Disease in the Jackson Heart Study." American Journal of Preventive Medicine (2019).</li>
      <li>Metayer, J. Graduate thesis, MS in Organization Development, Pepperdine Graziadio Business School (2026).</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
